course: dictionary
lesson: 12591
title: Paying money out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When money leaves a fund, a charity or a bank to pay for something, we say it is disbursed. Disburse is a formal word, so you will meet it in letters, forms and maths questions. «The charity disburses grants to local schools every spring.» The charity pays money out to the schools.
explain: Look for clues. Who is paying, and where does the money come from? If the money comes from a fund, a charity, a bank or an organisation, then disburse means to pay it out. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "pay out" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, money that is disbursed leaves the fund, so the amount left goes down. «The fund had 500 pounds. It disbursed 120 pounds to the club.» The fund now has only 380 pounds left.
fact: Disburse means to pay money out, usually from a fund.
fact: Disburse is a formal word, so you will find it in official letters and business reports.
fact: «The school disbursed the prize money to the winners.» means the school paid the prize money out.
fact: When money is disbursed, the amount in the fund goes down.
fact: Useful phrases: disburse funds, disburse payments.
exercise: «The council disburses money to repair the park.» What does disburses mean? | Earns money from the park | *Pays money out | Keeps money safe for ever | Counts money in a bank
exercise: «The fund had 500 pounds and disbursed 120 pounds.» How much is left in the fund? | 500 pounds | 620 pounds | 120 pounds | *380 pounds
exercise: Which phrase is the best match for disburse funds? | Lose the funds | Keep funds locked away | Count the funds at night | *Pay out funds
test: «The charity disbursed grants to three schools.» What did the charity do with the grants? | Hid them in a box | Asked for them back | Lost them in the post | *Paid them out
test: Ravi says disburse means to save money in a piggy bank. Is he right? | Yes, it means to count coins | No, it means to borrow money | Yes, it means to save coins | *No, it means to pay money out from a fund
exam: «The bank disburses the loan to Mr Chen.» Which phrase means the same as disburses? | Hides | Asks for back | Locks away | *Pays out
